@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<n>&cursor=<cursor>` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "..."}`: items are ordered by ascending `id`. `limit` is an integer from 1 to 100 and defaults to 20. The cursor is the string ID of the last item in the previous page; omit it for the first page. `next_cursor` is the last item's ID when more items remain and `null` at the end. Invalid limits or cursors return HTTP 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
